% Problem 22. Chace vol. II pl. 45 (photograph XI, register 2), PDF pp. 137-138; Peet p. 59 (pl. H).
No. 22
"Complete 2/3 '30 as 1."
"20 1"                  % beneath 2/3 and '30, their values in 30ths; no total written. Black in Chace; Peet prints them in italics (his sign for red)
"The total of the excess of it is: 9."
Reckon with 30 to find 9.   % "Operate on 30 for the finding of 9."
  1     30
\ '10   3
\ 5     6               % 5 for '5; Chace fn 2: "The scribe omitted the fractional dot."
Total 9.
"Therefore '5 '10 is: to be added to it."
"Therefore is complete 2/3 5 '10 '30 up to 1."   % 5 for '5 here too; Chace fn 2: "The scribe omitted the fractional dot."
"20 6 3 1"              % beneath 2/3 '5 '10 '30, their values in 30ths; no total written. Black in Chace; Peet prints them in italics (his sign for red)
